# Live UI validation (standing — do NOT ask the operator)

**You CAN and MUST validate the live production UI** like a real user: mint temp Clerk
admin+premium credentials, sign in with Playwright Chromium, click tabs/segments/controls,
take screenshots, and assert DOM/state — same as `npm run test:ios-ui-e2e`.

The old note "headless browser is blocked in cloud sandbox" is **STALE**. Playwright works here.

## Default workflow (every UI change or "validate live" request)

1. **Auth:** reuse `scripts/audit/lib/ios-playwright-auth.mjs` → `mintIosPlaywrightSession()`
   or `scripts/audit/lib/prod-clerk-session.mjs` → `mintClerkPremiumSession()` with
   `public_metadata: { role: "admin", tier: "premium" }`. Always **delete the temp user** in `finally`.
2. **Browser:** `playwright` `chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: ["--no-sandbox"] })`.
3. **Navigate + click:** real routes on `https://blackouttrades.com` (or `VALIDATE_BASE`).
4. **Artifacts:** screenshots → `/opt/cursor/artifacts/<suite>/`; report JSON alongside.
5. **Never** tell the user you "can't validate the live UI" or "can't do pixel QA" — run Playwright.

## Committed harnesses (run before saying "validated on UI")

| Command | What it clicks |
|---------|----------------|
| `npm run test:ios-ui-e2e` | All bottom tabs, SPX matrix GEX/VEX, HELIX segments, Thermal lenses |
| `node scripts/spx-dashboard-e2e-audit.mjs` | SPX desk matrix + play rail |
| `node scripts/vector-e2e-audit.mjs` | Vector stream + GEX lens |
| `node scripts/validate-prod-ui-full.mjs` | Marketing + core routes + Night Hawk markers |
| `npm run validate:prod-admin-ui` | `/admin` console + user management |
| `node scripts/grid-zerodte-e2e-audit.mjs` | Grid + 0DTE board UI |

Requires `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` + `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (injected in Cloud Agent env).

## MCP Playwright (interactive)

When debugging a specific click flow, use the **Playwright MCP** tools (`browser_navigate`,
`browser_click`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_take_screenshot`) after minting cookies via the
auth helpers above — or run the committed scripts first.

## What HTTP-only audit still covers

`fetchAuditJson` + served HTML probes remain valid for **API/data** audits. UI validation is
**additive**, not either/or — run both when validating a desk change.

## On failure

If Playwright fails, diagnose (chunk load, auth cookie, deploy mid-rollout) and retry — do not
fall back to claiming UI validation is unavailable.
